      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "High glycemic index foods cause a rapid spike in blood sugar and a sharp insulin response, which places extra demand on your body's ability to manage glucose. In contrast, low glycemic index foods release sugar slowly, resulting in a more gradual insulin rise that helps avoid the peaks and troughs often seen in type 2 diabetes. Prioritizing low GI foods can therefore stabilize your blood glucose levels, reduce insulin resistance, and lower the risk of further damage to your heart and arteries.",
